# @speculos-harness/bundler — the locked-down build-service container.
#
# PRE-RELEASE: this is a stub, not a working Dockerfile. It documents the shape of the
# hardened image that ships as `speculos/harness-bundler` with the v0.1 code drop. It is
# named Dockerfile.stub (not Dockerfile) on purpose so nothing tries to build it today.
# At v0.1 it becomes a real, published, multi-stage build.
#
# WHY THIS IS A CONTAINER AND NOT JUST A LIBRARY
# ----------------------------------------------
# `bun add` runs arbitrary npm, and Bun.build resolves the app's imports against this
# box's own node_modules. That means the build service is the one component that
# executes untrusted dependency code. It is shipped ONLY as this locked-down image so a
# naive setup (root, install scripts enabled, temp dir moved out from under cwd) cannot
# turn a bundle request into remote code execution. A startup self-check refuses to boot
# if any invariant below is misconfigured away.
#
# THE INVARIANTS THE v0.1 IMAGE WILL ENFORCE
# ------------------------------------------
#   * Runs as a NON-ROOT user (a dedicated unprivileged account, never UID 0).
#   * All installs run with --ignore-scripts, always — a package cannot execute
#     install-time scripts on the build box. This flag is not configurable off.
#   * Package name and version are regex-validated before they ever reach `bun add`.
#   * Builds happen in an EPHEMERAL directory UNDER the process cwd (load-bearing: it is
#     what lets node_modules resolve) and are wiped per request.
#   * The base dependency set the system prompt promises is BAKED at image build time
#     (react 19, recharts, @tanstack/react-table, date-fns, lucide-react, ...), from the
#     same single list the prompt's LIBRARIES block is generated from; a startup
#     self-check asserts every promised package resolves.
#   * Only the bundler port is exposed; no secrets are baked into the image.
#
# INTENDED SHAPE (illustrative — not runnable until v0.1)
# -------------------------------------------------------
#
#   FROM oven/bun:1 AS base
#   # Create and switch to an unprivileged user; the build never runs as root.
#   RUN useradd --create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin bundler
#   WORKDIR /home/bundler/app
#
#   # Bake the promised base dependencies with --ignore-scripts, generated from one list.
#   COPY base-package.json ./package.json
#   RUN bun install --ignore-scripts
#
#   # The sidecar source (the serve() entrypoint from src/index.ts).
#   COPY --chown=bundler:bundler dist ./dist
#
#   USER bundler
#   EXPOSE 8081
#   # The entrypoint runs the startup self-check FIRST and exits non-zero if any
#   # invariant above is violated, then starts the server.
#   CMD ["bun", "dist/serve.js"]
#
# See spec/bundle.md and spec/security.md for the normative bundle contract and the
# non-negotiable build-service safety rules.
